      ":question/problem": "Using the formal definition, prove that\n\n$lim_(n \u2192 \u221e)\\sqrt{n + 1} = \u221e$.\n\nWe need to show that for any real $M > 0$, there exists a natural number $N$ such that, for every natural number $n \\ge N$, we have\n$\\sqrt{n + 1} > M$.\n\nSolving this inequality for $n$, we get\n$>$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}\n\nTherefore, we choose $N$\n{{field-3}} {{field-4}}."
